Carafe Lab: an OpenGL image view whose format orders red and blue the other way than its image's format exchanges red
and blue in its swizzle. OpenGL has no BGR view formats, so glTextureView of an A8B8G8R8 image as B8G8R8A8 read the
image's bytes in their stored order, where the Vulkan renderer's view format reorders them: Hitman 2: Silent
Assassin's menu pictures and scenery came out blue where they are red.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/src/video_core/renderer_opengl/gl_texture_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_opengl/gl_texture_cache.cpp
@@ -195,6 +195,17 @@
     return dst_format == src_format || (!IsPackedFormat(dst_format) && !IsPackedFormat(src_format));
 }

+[[nodiscard]] u8 SwapRedBlue(u8 source) {
+    switch (static_cast<SwizzleSource>(source)) {
+    case SwizzleSource::R:
+        return static_cast<u8>(SwizzleSource::B);
+    case SwizzleSource::B:
+        return static_cast<u8>(SwizzleSource::R);
+    default:
+        return source;
+    }
+}
